Origin of the files in this directory
=====================================

frsqrte_pairs.txt, fres64_pairs.txt, fres32_pairs.txt
    Input/output bit pairs of the Gekko `frsqrte` and `fres` instructions,
    one pair per line as `<input_hex> <output_hex>` (16 hex digits for the
    double-width files, 8 for fres32), sorted by input bits.

    They were captured by executing the instructions inside Dolphin (Felk's
    scripting fork, interpreter core) with a hand-assembled guest program and
    no game disc; see harness/gekko_probe/README.md. No emulator source was
    consulted; the pairs are observed behaviour. The ARM64 JIT capture agreed
    on every numeric pair and differed only by quieting signalling-NaN
    inputs, which these files do not reflect (they follow the interpreter).

    fres32 pairs are `lfs` / `fres` / `stfs` (single in, single out);
    frsqrte and fres64 pairs are `lfd` / op / `stfd` (double in, double out).

    The full captures (~74k pairs) live under harness/traces/ and are not
    committed. These files are a deterministic subset chosen by
    harness/gekko_probe/select_fixture.py: every special value, every table
    index with a spread over the linear-term bits, the fres clamp
    neighbourhoods, and random fill. tests/golden.rs replays every pair
    against gekko_math::estimate, and also replays the full captures when
    present.

    The decision to commit tables and pairs derived from these captures is
    recorded in TRACKER.md (user decision, 2026-09-08).
